Ray Brown has first-position dlines in center field and at pitcher, and Jerry
Benjamin has first-position dlines at catcher and in right field, though
Tommie Dukes caught all 27 outs. The pline records list Joe Strong, Willie
Gisentaner, and Brown as the first, second, and third pitchers, but the dline
pitcher sequence is Brown, Strong, Gisentaner. Tom Parker's dline is the
second right fielder. So Brown started in center field and finished on the
mound, Benjamin moved from right field to center field, and Parker took right
field. Benjamin's catcher dline (2 putouts) becomes the second center fielder,
Benjamin's start record gets position 9, and the pitcher dline sequence follows the
pline order.

